---
// "Zero-friction capture" band: the four capture commands (todo/bug/seed/quick).
---

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Zero-friction capture</span>
    <h2 class="h2">Something surfaces? One line, keep going</h2>
    <p class="sub">Work turns up mid-flow all the time. Record it in a single command and it lands as a real ticket, not a lost thought, without derailing the ticket you're on.</p>
    <div class="captures">
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-head"><span class="tag todo">todo</span><span class="cmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>todo</span></div>
        <p>A <b>small, defined build ticket</b> you'll do now. Straight onto the board, scoped and ready to work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-head"><span class="tag bug">bug</span><span class="cmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>bug</span></div>
        <p>A <b>defect</b>, captured with its repro. Add <code>--of</code> to mark it a regression of an already-shipped ticket.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-head"><span class="tag seed">seed</span><span class="cmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>seed</span></div>
        <p>Work <b>parked until a future trigger</b> fires. Kept blocked and auditable, so nothing wanted-later slips through the cracks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cap">
        <div class="cap-head"><span class="tag quick">quick</span><span class="cmd"><span class="s">/trailhead:</span>quick</span></div>
        <p>Work one loose ticket <b>whole, off the map</b>, start to finish. Grills only if needed, never splits, just get it done.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
